WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.300
- Surgeon Simulator, Amateur Surgeon,

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.810
Plague Inc., Bio Inc.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:08.240
Now comes, Operate Now: Hospital Edition?

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:10.020
You recommended it, I'm about to play it.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.143
Let's get it started.

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:11.976
Bewoop!

00:00:11.976 --> 00:00:14.840
In a hospital, every day is
a matter of life and death.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:16.060
Sounded super dramatic.

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:17.300
Doctor I know you're new here,

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.730
but this is no time for niceties.

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:20.563
Niceties?

00:00:20.563 --> 00:00:22.070
What's your name, doctor?

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:22.910
This is easy.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.010
Dr. Mike, and I love that
doctor is spelled out.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.420
I don't know if you guys
notice, on all my stuff,

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.610
I spell out, well, not on this one, but.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:30.790
Gaping wound.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:32.540
Very easy, two minutes.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:35.530
Okay doctor, we need to make
neat stitches across the wound.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:36.363
Bam.

00:00:36.363 --> 00:00:37.196
Bam.

00:00:37.196 --> 00:00:39.513
God, I like using the pencil for this.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.394
100%.

00:00:42.394 --> 00:00:45.090
Let's put the applicator tool.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:45.923
Good work, doctor.

00:00:45.923 --> 00:00:47.130
He's stabilizing, perhaps now

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.970
I can introduce myself properly.

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:49.803
I'm Amy.

00:00:49.803 --> 00:00:51.900
Dr. Stone told me you were in charge

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:52.950
until he return.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.070
Amy!

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:55.240
Why did no one,

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.670
why did no one let me
know about the newcomer

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:59.040
being put in charge?

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.090
Patients lives hang on
by a thread and I have to

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.650
wait on an amateur to sign
off on my operating room?

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.410
God, it's like Grey's Anatomy episode.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:07.299
You don't have to talk to Dr. Mike

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:09.810
as if they weren't here, Sirona.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.121
What do you say about getting
things running, doctor?

00:01:12.121 --> 00:01:14.321
All right, what should
we name the hospital?

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:16.430
What about like,

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:19.316
Happy and Healthy Memorial.

00:01:19.316 --> 00:01:20.149
(laughs) That's corny.

00:01:20.149 --> 00:01:24.493
Dat Healthy Spot, Yo.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:27.760
Here you'll find a list of
available tasks such as:

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:29.730
Surgeries, assignments, and more.

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:30.563
Okay.

00:01:30.563 --> 00:01:32.223
I gotta build the operating room.

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:35.890
Building different departments will keep

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:37.700
your hospital running
and allow you to produce

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:38.600
the resources that you need.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.250
Okay, I like that, let's go then.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.880
We have a level one
operating room installed,

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.680
wow that's a nice operating room.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.120
Dangerous Polyp?

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.710
Difficulty very easy.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:50.543
Okay, doctor.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:52.580
Now that we have good sanitary
conditions to operate in,

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:55.160
let's see how you perform
a complex surgery.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:57.820
I don't know of a polyp is
considered a complex surgery,

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.690
Oh, but it's in the intestines.

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:01.100
A polyp ectomy.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.920
Any time you have a term in medicine,

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.480
where you have ectomy,

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:06.760
that means you're talking it out.

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:09.126
Appendectomy, taking out the appendix.

00:02:09.126 --> 00:02:10.463
Polypectomy, taking out the polyp.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.270
You get what I'm saying?

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:18.233
First we need to apply the
anti-septic tool applicator,

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.013
which is really true.

00:02:21.013 --> 00:02:22.080
This is the first thing that we do.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.660
Then we get the scalpel.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:25.210
Then, because I have my awesome pencil,

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:27.110
I can just do a perfect
incision right there.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:29.100
Look at that, it's like I've
been doing this my whole life.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.330
Take too long, or make mistakes

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:31.200
and you'll lose the patient.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.033
Don't stop now.

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:32.866
Scalpel.

00:02:32.866 --> 00:02:34.450
Let's go right into.

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:37.414
This is almost like an
exploratory laparotomy,

00:02:37.414 --> 00:02:39.470
but it's a little bit deeper than this.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:40.530
Now we can see the polyp.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:41.423
Let's laser it.

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:44.563
Oh it's good.

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:50.223
Promote healing by applying
gel over the cauterized area.

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:52.980
Now, let's suture.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:53.813
Bam.

00:02:53.813 --> 00:02:54.646
Bam.

00:02:54.646 --> 00:02:55.479
Bam.

00:02:55.479 --> 00:02:56.312
Look at that.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.320
Good, now let's close her
up while we still have time.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.680
Select the needle tool.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:02.540
Bop.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:03.430
Bop.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:04.263
Bop.

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.550
And we cleaned it up.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:10.170
She said my stitching needs work,

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:12.370
but a competent job, I suppose.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.550
I think she's just hating,
that operation was a success.

00:03:15.550 --> 00:03:16.383
I'm the man.

00:03:16.383 --> 00:03:17.930
By the way, this new game I'm addicted to,

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:19.410
I kinda gave up on Overwatch.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.030
It's called Apex Legends.

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:23.460
If you want me to play
Season 2 Apex Legends,

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:26.330
'cause I'm nasty, drop it
down below in the comments.

00:03:26.330 --> 00:03:28.220
Hospital Life, there are
three departments types

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.120
for you to manage.

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.780
An admission department admits patients.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.730
These indicators tell you
how much cash you have,

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:36.490
how many beds are in use.

00:03:36.490 --> 00:03:37.860
Tap on medical departments

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.890
to collect the cash that accumulates.

00:03:39.890 --> 00:03:41.320
Here, you'll be able to manage your staff

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.020
and assign them based on their specialty,

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:44.670
thus allowing your
departments to function.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:45.720
All right, let's see.

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:49.310
I have one angry surgeon here.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:50.730
With Sirona assigned
to the operating room,

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:52.050
we'll have steady cash flow.

00:03:52.050 --> 00:03:53.110
Let's claim it.

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:54.260
Boom.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:55.093
What did I earn?

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.350
(chuckles) that was exciting.

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:00.653
I got Dr. Ambrosia,

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:05.560
and she gives me 1% extra
money, and 1% extra time?

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:06.410
I don't know what that means.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.610
We'll need a place where
patients can recover safely.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:09.443
Let's build a ward.

00:04:09.443 --> 00:04:11.633
Okay ward, $10,000.

00:04:11.633 --> 00:04:14.203
I have 27,000 let's build it right there.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.323
I have 23 beds, and I got another reward.

00:04:19.924 --> 00:04:21.910
I got John, the Nurse.

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:26.910
I'm gonna put my nurse in
there, in the recovery area.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:28.420
Build a break room.

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:29.253
Let's do it.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.580
I still don't get the need for that.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.230
Resource spending should be
solely for better patient care.

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:38.310
Well, Serona, I hate to be
the one to tell you this,

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.980
but in order to be more productive,

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:41.300
you need to be well rested.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.660
In order to be well rested,

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.030
you need to have some quiet time.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:45.550
Silence is golden.

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:47.110
We need a break room.

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:50.028
For nurses, for doctors, and residents.

00:04:50.028 --> 00:04:51.340
Well, the residents are probably

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:53.240
not gonna get access until
they start complaining

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:54.400
and all that stuff, but you know.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.480
Doubt much resting will take place there.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.790
Those hooligans will turn
it into a frat house.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:04:59.623
What hooligans?

00:04:59.623 --> 00:05:01.890
We have like three staff in my hospital

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:06.234
that's called, Dat Spot
Where You'll Get Healthy, Yo.

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:08.102
(chuckles) If assigned staff
member runs out of stamina,

00:05:08.102 --> 00:05:09.850
the department will stop working.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:12.640
Refill their stamina, assign
them to the break room

00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:15.970
or simply put another non-tired
staff member to work there.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:16.900
Okay.

00:05:16.900 --> 00:05:18.830
Oh my God, I can give him plus 50 energy

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:19.980
by giving him coffee.

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.370
Here's some coffee buddy.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:23.890
And look, my staff is
already performing better,

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.810
and we got another reward.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:28.270
This game has the most
rewards I've ever seen.

00:05:28.270 --> 00:05:32.160
Energy drink, recovers 100
stamina points instantly.

00:05:32.160 --> 00:05:33.410
There should be a little
thing at the bottom,

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.040
but shortens your life just a bit.

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:35.990
Work is relentless.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:38.050
A patient has come in with
a severe bone fracture.

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:39.820
Care to take a look?

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:41.070
I don't mind taking a look.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:44.030
Jake, 21, went on a night out.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:47.810
He fell off his bike riding
home, and broke his right arm.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:48.643
Ouch.

00:05:48.643 --> 00:05:50.160
The scaphoid wrist bone
is usually the most

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.740
commonly broken bone when you're falling

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:52.860
on an out stretched hand.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:54.462
That's the one that's more in your wrist.

00:05:54.462 --> 00:05:58.140
This, the area looks like
we're going into, is either

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:01.140
an ulna fracture or a radial fracture.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:02.440
I'm gonna go ahead and guess ulna.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:03.273
I don't know why.

00:06:03.273 --> 00:06:05.100
I'm just, where it is,

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:05.933
I don't know.

00:06:05.933 --> 00:06:06.830
Let's just clean it up.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:10.170
Let's go.

00:06:10.170 --> 00:06:11.690
Bop.

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:13.370
Clean incision.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.033
It's worse than we thought, yeah.

00:06:20.136 --> 00:06:21.986
Yeah, let's get the bones outta here.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.430
Good work, I've cleaned the fragments.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:28.463
Now I need you to reassemble the bones.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:35.250
Look at that.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.320
Now let's place the metal support.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:38.153
Bop.

00:06:38.153 --> 00:06:41.930
That's called an open reduction
internal fixation procedure.

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:42.800
ORIF.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.500
Basically, open, meaning
we had to cut open

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:48.150
the person's body in
order to make this happen.

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:50.600
And internal fixation
means that we had to put

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:54.970
metal hardware in there
to make the bones stay.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.280
Yay, operation successful!

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:57.340
We could have done it a little faster,

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:59.120
if I wasn't narrating the procedure.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:02.940
I'm tryin' to teach you how
to do a radial fracture,

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:03.790
or ulna fracture.

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:04.740
I didn't really pay attention.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.040
Not good to say as a doctor.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:08.100
Dr. Stone, judging by the
hospital's reputation,

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:11.460
the new doctor's certainly
living up to my expectations.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:12.530
I guess he doesn't know what I named

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:13.510
the hospital, thank God.

00:07:13.510 --> 00:07:15.040
Fracture, left leg.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:18.950
Your patient has a comminuted
break on the tibia, ow!

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.970
That's the lower part, the shin bone.

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:22.440
All right, let's do it.

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:24.850
We're gonna start by cleaning, yes.

00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:26.703
Then by scalpeling, bam.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:30.809
Okay, now that we're inside,

00:07:30.809 --> 00:07:33.080
the tibia doesn't look so good.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:35.420
We gotta get these cleaned up,

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:36.833
so let's put them up there.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:39.513
Thank you.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:43.163
Okay.

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:45.493
Okay.

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:50.463
Okay.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.468
I feel like I'm a real
doctor or something.

00:07:54.468 --> 00:07:57.135
(calming music)

00:07:59.190 --> 00:08:00.640
This is fun.

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:01.900
Good job Dr. Mike.

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:06.350
I will say, this game
is extremely, accurate,

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:08.770
because I'm legitimately stressed out,

00:08:08.770 --> 00:08:12.000
I feel like I have to
deal with PR, bosses,

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:16.180
patients, staff members,
their needs, their training.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:18.060
I mean, I loved playing
Sims back in the day,

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:19.280
but that was stressful.

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:21.620
What I want you to learn from this is A,

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:23.480
how complicated it is to run hospital.

00:08:23.480 --> 00:08:24.640
You have all these things,

00:08:24.640 --> 00:08:26.810
you need to constantly upgrade equipment,

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:31.270
make choices, difficult choices,
not put a break room in,

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:34.690
upgrade a break room, give
staff members free coffee,

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:36.500
don't upgrade the caf, I mean.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:39.200
I prefer Bio Inc. and
Plague Inc. to this one.

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.070
I just feel like it's more mischievous,

00:08:41.070 --> 00:08:42.600
and I can have more fun
playing those games.

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:43.810
This feels like work.

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:47.710
If you wanna see some more
of my game-playing videos,

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:50.290
click on this playlist
right here, and as always,

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:52.435
stay happy and healthy.

